"Let $\\mathcal{G}$ be an oligomorphic permutation group on a set $G$, and let $\\mathbb{G}$ be a countable smooth digraph of algebraic length $1$ on $G$ that is invariant under $\\mathcal{G}$. A **pseudoloop** is an edge obtained from a loop by applying elements of $\\mathcal{G}$ to its endpoints. **Pseudoloop lemma conjecture.** Either $\\mathbb{G}$ contains a pseudoloop, or $\\mathbb{G}$ together with the orbits of $\\mathcal{G}$ on finite tuples pp-interprets $\\mathbb{K}_3$ with parameters, where $\\mathbb{K}_3=(\\{1,2,3\\};\\neq)$. This would generalize the finite loop lemma to the stated infinite, invariant-digraph setting; the conjecture is presented as open in the source."